From: Antoni Sawicki <as@tenoware.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cgthree: map only the console lines that fit, for screens of
 any size

OpenBIOS has 768 KB of address space to map a frame buffer in, which
is the size of 1024 x 768. The FCode ROM of the cg3 mapped that much
and then drew on the whole screen, so at 1152 x 900 OpenBIOS took a
data access fault when it cleared the screen, and the machine hung
with a blank window.

The ROM now maps the lines at the top of the screen that fit, and the
firmware's text console uses those: 682 lines at 1152 x 900, 409 at
1920 x 1080. The width, height and linebytes properties still give
the real size, and SunOS maps all of the frame buffer by itself, so
OpenWindows and SunView use the whole screen.

Origin: https://github.com/tenox7/lemu/commit/9ea85e132e43d55422f8d527e9dfc74bca33aa59
---
diff --git a/drivers/cgthree.fs b/drivers/cgthree.fs
index aa0c90c..0960cc1 100644
--- a/drivers/cgthree.fs
+++ b/drivers/cgthree.fs
@@ -79,7 +79,20 @@ h# 400000 constant cg3-off-dac
 h# 20 constant /cg3-off-dac
 
 h# 800000 constant cg3-off-fb
-h# c0000 constant /cg3-off-fb
+
+\
+\ OpenBIOS has 768 KB of address space left to map a frame buffer in, which
+\ is the size of 1024 x 768. The "width" and "height" properties give the
+\ operating system the real size, and it maps all of the frame buffer by
+\ itself. The firmware's own text console uses the lines at the top of the
+\ screen that fit in what OpenBIOS can map.
+\
+
+h# c0000 constant /cg3-console
+
+: console-height ( -- lines )
+  /cg3-console line-bytes / openbios-video-height min
+;
 
 : >cg3-reg-spec ( offset size -- encoded-reg )
   >r 0 my-address d+ my-space encode-phys r> encode-int encode+
@@ -132,7 +145,7 @@ headerless
 ;
 
 : fb-map
-  cg3-off-fb h# c0000 do-map-in to fb-addr
+  cg3-off-fb line-bytes console-height * do-map-in to fb-addr
 ;
 
 : map-regs
@@ -161,7 +174,7 @@ headerless
 
     frame-buffer-adr encode-int " address" property
 
-    openbios-video-width openbios-video-height over char-width / over char-height /
+    openbios-video-width console-height over char-width / over char-height /
     fb8-install
   then
 ;
